ely D expert ratings support a Democratic margin near seven points.", "watch": "A late debate stumble or external spending surge for James could tighten the race toward Lean D territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Gretchen Whitmer (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's open governor's race pits Democrat Jocelyn Benson against Republican John James, with term limits keeping Gretchen Whitmer off the ballot. Polling through late September consistently shows Benson ahead, with independent pollsters reporting leads of five to seventeen points and even Republican-leaning surveys showing a single-digit race. Averages place the margin near seven to nine points.\n\nBenson has more than doubled James's fundraising and holds a large cash-on-hand edge. Markets price her win probability above ninety percent, and expert raters uniformly lean Democratic, with one calling it Likely D. The state's even partisan baseline is outweighed by the 2026 environment and the money gap, pointing to a clear but not insurmountable Benson advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9339, "margin": 7.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9166, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9224, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9053, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9221, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9131, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 7.0}]}